4. PREBUILT BINARIES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The binaries in Linux/libcarla-install/lib/ are prebuilt for Linux x86-64 and
map to components as follows:

  libcarla_client.a                              CARLA (MIT)
  librpc.a                                       rpclib (MIT) + msgpack-c
  libboost_atomic.a, .so.1.84.0                  Boost (BSL-1.0)
  libboost_filesystem.a, .so.1.84.0              Boost (BSL-1.0)
  libboost_program_options.a, .so.1.84.0         Boost (BSL-1.0)
  libboost_python38.a, .so.1.84.0                Boost (BSL-1.0)
  libboost_system.a, .so.1.84.0                  Boost (BSL-1.0)
  libRecast.a                                    Recast (Zlib)
  libDetour.a                                    Detour (Zlib)
  libDetourCrowd.a                               Detour (Zlib)
  libDetourTileCache.a                           Detour (Zlib)
  libDebugUtils.a                                Recast Navigation (Zlib)
  libpng16.a, .so.16.37.0, .la                   libpng (Libpng)

IMPORTANT: libcarla_client.a is a static archive that statically embeds compiled
third-party object code, not only CARLA's own. Symbol inspection of the archive
finds code from Boost, rpclib, pugixml, odrSpiral and moodycamel::ConcurrentQueue.
Anyone linking against it is redistributing those components too, and the notices
in this file and in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES/ travel with them.

libpng16.la records "dependency_libs=' -lz -lm'": zlib is NOT bundled here and is
resolved from the system at link time. Its license is therefore out of scope for
this repository.


